    {
      "title": "CJI turns down Congress's meeting request; Opposition march to SC today",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/politics/opposition-to-march-to-supreme-court-today-over-vote-chori-cec-removal-126101200006_1.html",
      "description": "Intensifying their agitation against Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar, the opposition parties would march to the Supreme Court on Monday, with Congress' Rahul Gandhi and Mallikarjun Kharge seeking a meeting with Chief Justice of India (CJI) Surya Kant to raise the issue of \"vote chori\".\nThe Chief Justice, however, declined to meet Lok Sabha Leader of Opposition Rahul Gandhi over \"vote chori\" allegations, saying similar matters are sub judice in the Supreme Court, sources said.\nBoth Gandhi and Kharge had written to CJI Surya Kant, seeking a meeting between 4 and 5 pm on Monday to hand over a memorandum, demanding an end to \"vote chori\", CE Gyanesh Kumar's resignation, halting of Special Intensive Revision (SIR) of electoral rolls, and switching back to the paper ballot format.\nIn response to Rahul Gandhi's request for a meeting, CJI Surya Kant said on Sunday that no orders can be passed on the administrative side, as he asked the Congress leader to file a petition on the ...",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-12T02:12:23"
    },
    {
      "title": "Delhi Metro shuts entry, exit at 6 stations ahead of Opposition's march",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/delhi-metro-shuts-entry-exit-at-6-stations-ahead-of-opposition-s-march-126101200028_1.html",
      "description": "Entry and exit at six metro stations will remain closed from 6 am to 4 pm on Monday ahead of the Opposition's Supreme Court march, the Delhi Metro Rail Corporation (DMRC) said in a post on X.\nThe six metro stations where entry and exit will remain closed are - Patel Chowk, Janpath, Rajiv Chowk, Mandi House, Central Secretariat and Barakhamba Road, the DMRC said.\n\"The situation will be reviewed by the security agencies and necessary updates will be shared accordingly. However, interchange facility will remain available at all the concerned metro stations,\" it further said.\nThe opposition parties would march to the Supreme Court on Monday, with Congress' Rahul Gandhi and Mallikarjun Kharge seeking a meeting with Chief Justice of India (CJI) Surya Kant to raise the issue of alleged \"vote chori\".\nThe Chief Justice, however, declined to meet Lok Sabha Leader of Opposition Rahul Gandhi over \"vote chori\" allegations, saying similar matters are sub judice in the Supreme Court, sources said",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-12T02:10:37"
    },
    {
      "title": "CJI Surya Kant declines to meet Rahul Gandhi over 'vote chori' allegations",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/cji-surya-kant-declines-to-meet-rahul-gandhi-kharge-over-vote-chori-126101100813_1.html",
      "description": "Chief Justice of India Surya Kant has not agreed to meet Leaders of Opposition after both of them wrote to him seeking time for a meeting on Monday to raise the 'vote chori' issue, sources said on Sunday night.\nLeaders of Opposition (LoPs) in Lok Sabha and Rajya Sabha - Rahul Gandhi and Mallikarjun Kharge - had written to the CJI for a meeting with him between 4 and 5 PM on Monday to hand over a memorandum, demanding an end to 'vote chori', CEC Gyanesh Kumar's resignation, halting of SIR and switching back to paper ballot.\n\"Response of Hon'ble CJI to the letter received from Leaders of Opposition has been sent in their official mail,\" a source said.\nThe sources said that the CJI has not agreed to meet the LoPs. They did not elaborate further.\nOpposition parties have announced a protest march to the Supreme Court on Monday over their demands. The Congress is calling it  \"Chalo Delhi -  March for Democracy\" and said they would converge at 1.30 PM at Connaught Place-Barakhamba Road ..",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-11T17:19:44"
    }
  ]
}